      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "To which of the following sets do all the real numbers belong?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- The set ${Z}^{-}$ contains all the negative integer numbers. However, real numbers as, for instance, $\\sqrt{2}$ don't belong to ${Z}^{-},$ so ${Z}^{-}$ does *not* contain the real numbers. $\\,\\times$\n\n- The set $N$ contains all the natural numbers. However, real numbers as, for instance, $\\sqrt{2}$ don't belong to $N,$ so $N$ does *not* contain the real numbers. $\\,\\times$\n\n- The set $Q$ contains all the rational numbers. However, real numbers as, for instance, $\\sqrt{2}$ don't belong to $Q,$ so $Q$ does *not* contain the real numbers. $\\,\\times$\n\n- The set ${Q}^{-}$ contains all the negative rational numbers. However, real numbers as, for instance, $\\sqrt{2}$ don't belong to ${Q}^{-},$ so ${Q}^{-}$ does *not* contain the real numbers. $\\,\\times$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\"",
